## Summary
The article examines how enhanced executive compensation disclosure regulations may create an illusion of drastic salary reductions, such as a 93% cut for CEOs, due to changes in reporting standards. This illusion effect can distort perceptions of actual compensation adjustments, impacting corporate transparency.

## Key Points
- Strengthened executive compensation disclosure rules have been implemented.
- These rules can lead to misleading perceptions, such as apparent 93% salary cuts for CEOs.
- The 'illusion effect' indicates that reported changes may not reflect real compensation modifications.
- The implications for corporate governance and stakeholder understanding are highlighted.


